<task id="033" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-16b: Find view three-state gating and Run Index</title>
    <phase>3 Surfacing Spaarke</phase>
    <gate>032 complete (the similarity surface is per-row authorized), 015 complete (tab shell), 013 complete (client document identity)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies BFF handler code (`RagEndpoints` index-name resolution) and adds a new React view; tags include bff-api, frontend and fluent-ui; modifies `.tsx`. Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified work: the three states, the endpoint to call, the required `documentId` argument and the in-handler index-name fix are all named exactly. No architectural judgment remains after task 032.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>032,015,013</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, bff-api, office-addin, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build the Find tab's state machine. Similarity requires the open document to be indexed, and there is no on-demand embedding path, so the tab branches on three states derived from `sprk_searchindexed`. In the middle state the pane offers a **Run Index** button that calls the **existing** `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` — no new endpoint. Fix, in-handler, the fact that that route ignores per-record `sprk_searchindexname`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in React 19 + Fluent UI v9 inside an Office task pane, Office theme handling, and the BFF RAG indexing route. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>A `FindView` renders in both Word and Outlook and correctly selects one of three states from the resolved document identity and `sprk_searchindexed`. Run Index calls `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` passing `documentId`, and after the pipeline completes the view transitions to the results state. `RagEndpoints`' index-name resolution honors per-record `sprk_searchindexname`. The view is keyboard-navigable, announces state changes, and renders correctly in Office light and dark themes.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      **The three states (spec FR-16), driven by `sprk_searchindexed`, which is a Dataverse BIT — true / false / null gives exactly these three:**

      | State | Pane shows |
      |---|---|
      | No `sprk_document` (unsaved / external document) | "Save this document to Spaarke so it can be indexed for AI similarity search." + a link to the Save tab |
      | `sprk_document` exists, `sprk_searchindexed` is false or null | "This document isn't indexed yet." + a **Run Index** button |
      | `sprk_searchindexed` is true | Similarity results (owned by task 034) |

      **Run Index needs no new endpoint.** `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` already exists at `Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs:119` (handler at `:599`), carries JWT + `AddTenantAuthorizationFilter()` + the `ai-batch` limiter, takes `SendToIndexRequest { DocumentIds: List&lt;string&gt;, TenantId: string }` (`:1297`) and returns `SendToIndexResponse` (`:1313`) with per-document `SendToIndexDocumentResult` (`:1339`). It runs **OBO** (`IndexFileAsync(…, httpContext, …)` at `:702`) and **stamps `sprk_searchindexed` / `sprk_searchindexedon` at `:710-722`**.

      **The one defect to fix in-handler:** the index name comes from `searchIndexNameResolver.GetDefaultIndexName()` at `:632` and **ignores the per-record `sprk_searchindexname`**. That is a handler fix, not a new route.

      **Non-negotiable from `.claude/patterns/ai/indexing-pipeline.md`:** the call MUST pass `documentId` or chunks land as orphans and the tracking fields cannot be written; GUIDs must be lowercased; and an HTTP 200 carrying `ChunksIndexed = 0` is a **failure**, not a success — the UI must not report it as one.

      Related fields that exist on `sprk_document` and may be surfaced: `sprk_searchindexedon`, `sprk_searchindexqueuedon`, `sprk_searchindexcompletedon`, `sprk_searchindexname`, and the `sprk_ai_search_index` lookup.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/FindView.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/index.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/App.tsx</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/CreateTodoView.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/SaveView.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/RagSendToIndexIndexNameContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">Per-row authorization on the visualization similarity surface. Find must not be built on an unhardened surface; 032's measured per-row latency also sizes this view's result page.</dependency>
      <dependency task="015" status="pending">The Save | Find tab shell and the extended `NavigationTab` union that this view mounts into.</dependency>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Client document identity — whether a `sprk_document` exists for the open document, which selects between state 1 and states 2/3.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Run Index MUST call the existing `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index`. Do NOT create a new `/api/office` re-index endpoint — plan.md §3 records this as an answered open question.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every Run Index call MUST pass `documentId` (the `sprk_document` GUID, lowercased). Omitting it lands chunks as orphans and makes the tracking fields unwritable — per `.claude/patterns/ai/indexing-pipeline.md`, this is not optional and not recoverable after the fact.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">An HTTP 200 response carrying `ChunksIndexed = 0` MUST be surfaced in the pane as a **failure** state, not as success. Scope: the Run Index result handler in `FindView`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`sprk_searchindexed` is written by `RagIndexingJobHandler`, **never by the add-in**. The pane MUST NOT write that field, `sprk_searchindexedon`, or any other index-tracking field directly — it reads them and re-polls.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">Every Dataverse GUID crossing a boundary in this task (documentId sent to the index route, the identity read back) MUST be canonicalized to bare-lowercase via `cleanGuid`. Never interpolate a raw GUID into an OData key predicate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">All Find-tab UI uses Fluent UI v9 and MUST honor the Office light/dark theme via the existing `useOfficeTheme` hook. No hard-coded hex colors, no `Xrm`-bound components (NFR-03 — `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">Scope: this view lives in `src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/` and consumes `@spaarke/auth` only. The add-in does not depend on `@spaarke/ui-components` — recreate layouts per the r2 precedent and this project's documented Path-A exception. Do not add a dependency on the shared UI library.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10">Shared-first: the view lands in `shared/taskpane/` and any host difference is expressed through `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()`, not through `if (host === 'Word')` branching inside the view.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-11">The view MUST be keyboard-navigable and MUST announce each state transition via the existing `useAnnounce` pattern — including the transition into and out of the Run Index in-progress state.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">`POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` is modified by the index-name fix, so it MUST gain contract coverage asserting per-record `sprk_searchindexname` is honored. Banned: `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, DI-registration assertions, ctor null-check assertions, `Stopwatch` + `Task.Delay`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">This task touches the BFF, so publish size MUST be measured **against a fresh build of `origin/master`, not the recorded baseline number** — worktree a detached `origin/master`, publish both, zip BOTH with PowerShell `Compress-Archive`, and report both absolute sizes, the delta and the tool. Ceiling 60 MB; escalate at ≥+5 MB.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The PR description MUST carry a **Placement Justification** section per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` for the `RagEndpoints` handler change.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run `/conflict-check` before opening the BFF PR — `spaarkeai-compose-r8` and `unified-access-control-r2` are live on this hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">There is no `build:prod` script in `src/client/office-addins` — `npm run build` IS the production build. Install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Office task-pane view state machines; the Spaarke RAG indexing pipeline</topic>
    <files>
