    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="indexing-pipeline" location=".claude/patterns/ai/indexing-pipeline.md">Binding for the Run Index call: pass `documentId`, lowercase GUIDs, treat `ChunksIndexed = 0` as failure.</pattern>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins — apply for sizing, density and theme fit inside the narrow task pane.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md`, `spec.md` FR-16, `src/client/office-addins/CLAUDE.md`, and `.claude/patterns/ai/indexing-pipeline.md`. Read task 032's notes for the measured per-row latency. Emit the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL / sonnet / high). Run `/conflict-check`.</step>
    <step order="1">Read `RagEndpoints.cs:599-730` end to end — specifically `GetDefaultIndexName()` at `:632`, the OBO call at `:702` and the tracking stamp at `:710-722` — so the client is written against the route's real contract.</step>
    <step order="2">Fix the index-name resolution in-handler so a per-record `sprk_searchindexname` is honored and `GetDefaultIndexName()` is the fallback, not the only path. Add the contract test asserting this.</step>
    <step order="3">Build `FindView.tsx` with the three-state selector. State is derived from (a) whether task 013 resolved a `sprk_document` and (b) the BIT value of `sprk_searchindexed` — null and false both mean "not indexed yet".</step>
    <step order="4">Implement state 1 (no `sprk_document`): the copy from spec FR-16 plus a control that switches to the Save tab through the tab shell delivered by task 015.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement state 2 (not indexed): the copy plus the Run Index button. On click, call `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` with `{ DocumentIds: [lowercased documentId], TenantId }`, show an in-progress state, then re-read the identity/index state. Treat a 200 with `ChunksIndexed = 0` as a failure and say so.</step>
    <step order="6">Implement state 3 (indexed): render the results container that task 034 will fill. In this task it may be a minimal list — 034 owns lazy-scroll and the records bridge.</step>
    <step order="7">Wire `FindView` into `App.tsx` and the views barrel, gated by `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()` so both hosts get the same capability decision rather than a host-name branch.</step>
    <step order="8">Add unit tests for the three-state selector logic (true / false / null / no-document) in `shared/taskpane/components/views/__tests__/`.</step>
    <step order="9">Run `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` in `src/client/office-addins`; run `dotnet build` + `dotnet test` for the BFF change. Execute the `&lt;ui-tests&gt;` below in both hosts.</step>
    <step order="10">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the ADR-029 constraint; record both absolute sizes, the delta and the tool.</step>
    <step order="11">Update `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="12">Document any deviation in `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If honoring per-record `sprk_searchindexname` turns out to require changes beyond the `RagEndpoints` handler — a new resolver, a signature change on `IndexFileAsync`, or a change to `RagIndexingJobHandler` — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. plan.md §3 sizes this as an in-handler fix; if it is not, the sizing is wrong and the owner should decide.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Run Index returns HTTP 200 with `ChunksIndexed = 0` consistently for a document that ought to be indexable, STOP and escalate rather than presenting it to the user as success or silently retrying — that pattern is a known pipeline failure mode, not a UI concern.</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 032's measured per-row authorization latency makes the results state unusable at the default limit, STOP and escalate rather than raising the limit past what 032 authorized or bypassing the hardened path.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>No Find view exists in the add-in. `ls src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/` returns `CreateTodoView.tsx`, `SaveView.tsx`, `ShareView.tsx`, `SignInView.tsx`, `StatusView.tsx` — the closest neighbor is Outlook's unbuilt `search` placeholder tab, which has no view behind it. On the server side, `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` already exists at `Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs:119`, so no new endpoint is created.</existing>
    <extension>Yes on the server (the existing send-to-index route is extended in-handler, not replaced); No on the client (there is no view to extend — the `search` tab is a placeholder string in a union type with no component behind it).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without the three-state gate the Find tab either renders empty for every unindexed document with no explanation, or attempts a similarity query that cannot return anything — and the user has no way to get the document indexed from the pane, because the only trigger today is post-upload. The specific failing behavior is: open a Spaarke document that predates indexing, click Find, get a blank pane and no path forward.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="State 1 — unsaved document shows the save prompt">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a document in Word that has never been saved to Spaarke (a local desktop file).</step>
        <step>Open the Spaarke pane and select the Find tab.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane shows "Save this document to Spaarke so it can be indexed for AI similarity search." and a control that switches to the Save tab. No Run Index button appears. No similarity request is issued.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="State 2 — saved but unindexed shows Run Index">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Spaarke-sourced document whose `sprk_searchindexed` is null or false.</step>
        <step>Select the Find tab.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The pane shows "This document isn't indexed yet." and an enabled Run Index button. No results list renders.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Run Index transitions to results">
      <steps>
        <step>From state 2, click Run Index.</step>
        <step>Wait for the indexing pipeline to complete and the pane to re-read index state.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>An in-progress state is shown and announced; on completion `sprk_searchindexed` reads true and the view transitions to the results state. A 200 response with `ChunksIndexed = 0` instead surfaces an explicit failure message, not results and not a success toast.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark mode (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office host theme to dark (File → Account → Office Theme → Black, or the web host's dark setting).</step>
        <step>Reopen the pane and visit each of the three Find states.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>All text, buttons, borders and empty-state illustrations use Fluent v9 theme tokens and remain legible with adequate contrast in dark mode. No hard-coded light-mode colors bleed through in any of the three states.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Keyboard navigation and announcements (NFR-11)">
      <steps>
        <step>With the pane focused, navigate the Find tab using Tab / Shift+Tab / Enter only.</step>
        <step>Trigger Run Index from the keyboard and let it complete.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every interactive element is reachable and operable from the keyboard with a visible focus ring; each state transition (including entering and leaving the in-progress state) is announced via `useAnnounce`.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Outlook parity">
      <steps>
        <step>Repeat states 1 and 2 in the Outlook add-in.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The same states render, driven by `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()` rather than a host-name conditional; any capability legitimately absent in Outlook is gated, not silently broken.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">`npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build` in `src/client/office-addins` (there is no `build:prod` here — `build` IS production).</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test the BFF: `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/`, `dotnet test`.</tool>
    <tool name="git">`git worktree add` a detached `origin/master` for the publish-size comparison.</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/FindView.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/App.tsx</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Ai/RagEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/views/__tests__/FindView.test.tsx</output>
