  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the open document resolves to no `sprk_document`, when the Find tab renders, then it shows the save prompt and a link to the Save tab, and issues no similarity request.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a resolved `sprk_document` with `sprk_searchindexed` = null, when the Find tab renders, then it shows the "isn't indexed yet" copy and an enabled Run Index button.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a resolved `sprk_document` with `sprk_searchindexed` = false, when the Find tab renders, then it shows the same not-indexed state as null — false and null are not distinguished in the UI.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a resolved `sprk_document` with `sprk_searchindexed` = true, when the Find tab renders, then it shows the results state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Run Index is clicked, when the request is issued, then the request body contains the `sprk_document` GUID in `DocumentIds`, lowercased and brace-free, and the route called is `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` — asserted in a test, not by inspection.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given Run Index returns HTTP 200 with `ChunksIndexed = 0`, when the response is handled, then the pane shows an explicit failure state and does not transition to results.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a `sprk_document` with a non-null `sprk_searchindexname`, when `POST /api/ai/rag/send-to-index` processes it, then that index name is used and `GetDefaultIndexName()` is only the fallback — asserted by contract test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given an unauthenticated caller, when Run Index is invoked, then the request is rejected by the route's existing JWT + tenant filter and the pane surfaces an error state rather than an unhandled exception.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The add-in never writes `sprk_searchindexed`, `sprk_searchindexedon`, or any other index-tracking field — verified by grep over `src/client/office-addins/`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All six `&lt;ui-tests&gt;` pass, including the dark-mode and keyboard/announcement checks.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean and `npm run build` succeeds in `src/client/office-addins`; `dotnet build` and `dotnet test` are green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size was measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with PowerShell `Compress-Archive`; both absolute sizes, delta and tool are recorded; delta &lt;+5 MB and absolute &lt;60 MB.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-16 (the three-state table is quoted verbatim above) and the Owner Clarification "Require indexing first — removes the on-demand-embedding slow path entirely". plan.md §3 answers the spec's open question: Run Index needs no new endpoint. Task 034 owns the results themselves (lazy-scroll + the records bridge decision); this task owns the state machine and Run Index.
  </notes>

